15 0 obj
<< /A 41 0 R /Alt (Two histograms compare the percentage distribution of CDR3 lengths. Panel A shows data for alpacas and llamas, with alpacas in blue and llamas in red. Panel B illustrates alpacas and Bactrians, using the same color scheme. Both histograms display data ranging from 5 to 30 CDR3 lengths.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 31 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
16 0 obj
<< /A 42 0 R /Alt (Table and scatter plots depicting correlations between CDR3 length and charge or hydropathy for alpaca, llama, and bactrian species. The table shows correlation coefficients for different regions and species, highlighting significant values with asterisks. Scatter plots show negative correlations with lines of best fit, indicating relationships of CDR3 length with charge in panel B and hydropathy in panel C. Each plot includes an R value and significance level.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 32 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
17 0 obj
<< /A 43 0 R /Alt (Graphs and heatmaps display amino acid usage in CDR3 regions. Panels A, B, and C show amino acid usage percentages versus CDR3 length for different amino acids. Panels D, E, and F are heatmaps representing position-specific amino acid usage with varied intensities indicated by color, correlating with usage percentages along CDR3 lengths.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 33 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
18 0 obj
<< /A 44 0 R /Alt (Protein structure and interaction analysis image consisting of: A\) A 3D protein structure diagram with colored strands and loops. B-D\) Heat maps showing intensity variations with axes labeled CDR1 to CDR3. E\) Table comparing CDR3 interactions of species, listing alpaca/llama and camel, with numerical values and annotations like \215ns\216 and asterisks indicating significance across different parameters.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 34 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
19 0 obj
<< /A 45 0 R /Alt (Panel A shows density plots comparing FR2_CDR3_Dis between alpacas/llamas and camels with similar distributions. Panels B and C depict protein structures highlighting CDR3 in red. Panel D is a bar chart showing CDR3 length percentages for extended and bent structures. Panel E is a table detailing species-specific CDR3 interactions, structural properties, and solubility, with significant values marked by asterisks.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 35 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
20 0 obj
<< /A 46 0 R /Alt (Panel A shows a table comparing the number of contact residues and buried surface areas in different species. Panels B, C, D, and E illustrate graphical data: Panel B shows protein structures with specified CDR3 lengths and interface areas; Panel C depicts a negative correlation between CDR3 length and contact residues in VHH; Panel D shows a positive correlation for CDR3 contact residues; Panel E illustrates another negative correlation in FR2 contact residues. Correlation coefficients are provided with statistical significance.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 36 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
21 0 obj
<< /A 47 0 R /Alt (Table comparing amino acid class differences in epitopes and paratopes \(A\) and interaction types in VHH-Ag interfaces \(B\) for Alpaca/Llama and Camel. Values show differences, with statistically significant ones marked by asterisks. Colors highlight differences: red for positive and blue for negative values. Significance levels range from one to four asterisks, indicating increasing significance. \215ns\216 denotes not significant.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 37 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
